{"id":"n5-079","title":"こちら～ (kochira～)","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Refers to a person, place or thing; 'this', 'this one', 'this way', 'here'.","longExplanation":"The こちら grammar point is used to refer to a person, place, or thing that is closer to the speaker, or to show politeness when referring to someone. It can mean 'this', 'this one', 'this way', or 'here'.","formation":"こちら / こちら + の + Person/Thing","examples":[{"jp":"こちらは田中さんです。","romaji":"Kochira wa Tanaka-san desu.","en":"This is Mr./Ms. Tanaka.","words":[{"surface":"こちら","vocabId":"1004500","reading":"こちら"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"田中","vocabId":null},{"surface":"さん","vocabId":"1579350","reading":"さん"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"こちらのレストランは美味しいです。","romaji":"Kochira no resutoran wa oishii desu.","en":"This restaurant is delicious.","words":[{"surface":"こちら","vocabId":"1004500","reading":"こちら"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"レストラン","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"美味しい","vocabId":"1486650","reading":"おいしい"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"こちらへどうぞ。","romaji":"Kochira e douzo.","en":"Please come this way.","words":[{"surface":"こちら","vocabId":"1004500","reading":"こちら"},{"surface":"へ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"どうぞ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"こちらの方がいいですか、それともあちらの方がいいですか？","romaji":"Kochira no hou ga ii desu ka, sore to mo achira no hou ga ii desu ka?","en":"Is this one better, or is that one better?","words":[{"surface":"こちら","vocabId":"1004500","reading":"こちら"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"方","vocabId":"1516930","reading":"ほう"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いい","vocabId":null},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"それとも","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あちら","vocabId":null}